  "method": "Complete Glottolog languoid CSV; direct-parent edges from Glottolog v5.3 NEXUS plus all 27 dialect indexes. Separate WALS hierarchy. Exact Glottocode links only. No synthetic genealogical edges.",
  "limitations": [
    "No claim to include every language or every published classification worldwide.",
    "All 30 Phlorest catalogued dataset summary trees were imported; posterior tree samples were not imported.",
    "Entire Glottolog 5.3 node inventory and WALS classification snapshot retained. Underlying catalog bibliographies and all regional monographs are not fully ingested.",
    "Exact Glottocode identity only. Unmatched samples remain separate. Multiple samples of one Glottocode are preserved as source edge labels and excluded from automatic common-tip conflict detection.",
    "Computed topological incompatibility is not a judgment of scientific validity.",
    "Explicit paper-level debate currently curated for Transeurasian only; other debates remain unreviewed.",
    "Most languages lack a same-language label in the imported names dataset."
  ],
  "names_method": "All Glottolog names.csv rows retained with provider, language tag and original record ID. Names in the language itself are labels whose language tag matches the target ISO 639-3 code, using exact 639-1 to 639-3 equivalences only. These are source labels, not independently verified community autonyms. No macrolanguage or dialect inheritance.",
  "iso_mapping": {
    "source": "https://github.com/pycountry/pycountry/blob/main/src/pycountry/databases/iso639-3.json",
    "source_blob_sha": "3e9e69f1f5eafd71c12cb7b6464a39df53115e71",
    "note": "184 two-letter/three-letter equivalences extracted; source_blob_sha is a blob, not a commit URL. Repository file: https://github.com/pycountry/pycountry/blob/main/src/pycountry/databases/iso639-3.json"
  },
  "integrated_classifications": {
    "method": "Canonical IDs are exact Glottocodes; unknown samples and internal study clades retain source-specific IDs. Original sample labels remain on source-tagged edges. Tree hypotheses are never combined across sources as one asserted ancestry. Incompatibility is computed only between rooted summary topologies restricted to at least three shared, non-repeated, non-ancestor tip IDs. Sample absence and polytomies alone are not classified as conflict. Source-specific summary trees, not posterior samples, are imported.",
    "phlorest": "All 30 data repositories returned by the Phlorest organization repository search on 2026-10-12, excluding phlorest software and .github; second page empty.",
